{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולאדם לא מצא עזר", :translit "u'l'adam lo matza ezer", :gloss "but for Adam he did not find a help"} {:he "ולאדם אמר כי שמעת לקול אשתך", :translit "u'l'adam amar ki shamata l'kol ishtekha", :gloss "and to Adam He said because you listened to the voice of your wife"} {:he "ולאדם שלא עמל בו יתננו חלקו", :translit "u'l'adam she'lo amal bo yitnenu khal'ko", :gloss "and for Adam who did not toil in it, his lot shall be given"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולאדם לא מצא עזר" "ולאדם אמר כי שמעת לקול אשתך" "ולאדם שלא עמל בו יתננו חלקו"]}], :frame {:text "The verse Genesis 2:18 says it is not good for man to be alone and that God will make a helpmate for him. After naming all the animals Adam still lacks a counterpart (Genesis 2:20). God forms Eve and Adam receives her (Genesis 2:22-25). After eating from the tree God addresses Adam with punishment (Genesis 3:17) and decrees mortality (Genesis 3:19). The Ba'al HaTurim reads the three occurrences of ולאדם as a narrative arc: lacking a helper, receiving one, then being punished through her.", :sources ["Genesis 2:18" "Genesis 2:20" "Genesis 2:22" "Genesis 3:17" "Genesis 3:19"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ולאדם לא מצא עזר" "ולאדם אמר כי שמעת לקול אשתך" "ולאדם שלא עמל בו יתננו חלקו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ולאדם לא מצא עזר", :refs ["Genesis 2:20"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ולאדם אמר כי שמעת לקול אשתך", :refs ["Genesis 3:17"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ולאדם שלא עמל בו יתננו חלקו", :refs ["Ecclesiastes 2:21"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:05.852113135Z", :model "glm-5.2"}